docs/DESIGN-GUIDE.md:46:| `exec_command` | Execute arbitrary shell commands | Output parsing, scripting language support, interactive sessions |
docs/ROADMAP.md:7:Added the `search_code` MCP tool (#1825), the structural escalation tier between lexical search and full-file analysis. Two strict enum modes: `pattern` (structural code-pattern search with `$X` single-node and `$$$REST` variadic metavariables; Rust, Go, Python, and TypeScript) and `symbol` (definitions, callers, and implementors via an on-demand `StructuralGraph`, all supported languages). Results are byte-exact anchored spans suitable for `edit_replace`, cursor-paginated. The adoption gate tracks client/server error-rate, real-agent session share (new `session_origin` `MetricEvent` field), and the pre-registered v20 benefit ablation (#1824); also added `query_mode` and `result_count` metric fields.
